# The Last Warm Room — a lullaby that slowly goes wrong.
#
# Everything is the Cloud preset: a low drone, slow chords, and a ghost
# voice in mono that sighs between notes on a long glide, most often across
# a tritone. No high leads, nothing that pings. The unease is structural
# rather than loud: the chords sag flat against a drone that stays put, the
# tape warps harder as it goes, a felt-muffled heartbeat skips, and the
# germanium sits at 30-50% until the one moment it is allowed to break,
# after which everything is cut out from under the room and only its
# reverb is left. The ending detunes downward and never resolves.
#
# 60 bpm, so a beat is a second and the arithmetic below is in seconds.

bpm 60
gate 0.97
tail 4

# --- the bus, from the Cloud preset (per-track patches carry only the voice)
automate volume
0.393
automate spring
0
automate chorus_mode
0
automate reverb_tone
3500
automate reverb_pre
0.02
automate tape_flutter
0.346
automate tape_age
0.44

# Germanium: 30-50% as the piece darkens, then the one moment it matters.
automate fuzz
0.30 R:18 0.40:6@smooth 0.50:6@smooth 0.86:2@exp R:1.9 0.30:0.1@step R:2 0.36:6@smooth

# The tape warps harder as the piece goes wrong, relaxes after the cut,
# then sags again as the last chord dies.
automate tape_wow
0.34 R:16 0.62:14@smooth R:4 0.22:2@smooth 0.52:6@smooth
automate tape_drive
0.34 R:26 0.55:6@smooth R:2 0.30:0.1@step

# The room: it swallows the cut — wetter and longer the instant the
# instruments are pulled out, so the silence is the reverb's.
automate reverb_wet
0.38 R:33.9 0.62:0.1 R:4 0.45:4@smooth
automate reverb_decay
0.75 R:33.9 0.88:0.1

# --- the heart: a 909 kick tuned into the floor, under a felt blanket.
automate bd_level
0.3
automate bd_tune
0.08
automate bd_decay
0.62
automate bd_sweep
0.12
automate bd_attack
0.05
automate bd_drive
0
automate dr_drive
0
automate dr_tone
0.08

# --- drone: the one thing that never moves in pitch.
track drone vel=0.95 gain=2 patch=cloud reverb_send=0.15
D2:34 R:2 D2:6@0.6

automate drone.release
3 R:33.95 0.04:0.05 R:2 3:0.05

# --- pad: beautiful, then darker, then flat against the drone.
track pad vel=0.5 patch=cloud reverb_send=0.25
>6
[D3 F3 A3 E4]:6
[Bb2 D3 F3 A3 E4]:6
[G2 Bb2 D3 F#3 A3]:6
[Eb3 G3 Bb3 D4 A4]:6
[D3 Eb3 F3 A3 C4]:4@0.72
R:2
[D3 F3 A3 E4]:6@0.3

automate pad.glide
0.3
# The break has to land, not bloom: the one chord that strikes fast.
automate pad.attack
3.84 R:29.9 0.3:0.1@step R:4.1 3.84:0.05@step
automate pad.release
3 R:33.95 0.04:0.05 R:2 3:0.05
automate pad.cutoff
870 R:28 2600:4@exp R:2 700:0.05
automate pad.pitch_shift
0 R:20 -0.32:10@smooth R:4 0:0.05@step R:2 -0.7:6@smooth

# --- ghost: one voice in mono, sighing on a long glide. Mid register.
track ghost vel=0.42 patch=cloud reverb_send=0.4
>10
A3:2.5 Eb4:2 D4:1.5 R:2
F4:2 E4:1.5 Bb3:2.5 R:2
A3:2 G#3:2
D4:4
R:4
E4:2@0.3 Eb4:2@0.3

automate ghost.mono
1
automate ghost.glide
1.1
automate ghost.attack
1.2
automate ghost.release
2.5 R:33.95 0.04:0.05 R:2 2.5:0.05
automate ghost.cutoff
700 R:26 1400:4@exp R:2 700:0.05

# --- heart: lub-dub, a skipped beat as things turn, racing into the
# break, one lone beat in the silence, then slowing until it stops.
track heart kit=909 vel=0.5 gain=0.6 reverb_send=0.45
>4
(BD:0.28@0.55 BD:0.72@0.28)x14
R:1
(BD:0.28@0.6 BD:0.72@0.3)x7
(BD:0.25@0.7 BD:0.25@0.35 BD:0.25@0.72 BD:0.25@0.36)x8
R:1
BD:0.28@0.5 BD:0.72@0.25
BD:0.28@0.45 BD:1.72@0.22
BD:0.28@0.4 BD:2.72@0.2
BD:1@0.3
